// A cast to never, or through unknown, tells the compiler to stop checking the value: the
// expression then fits any type, so a wrong shape compiles. This refuses both; a value that
// needs a type the checker cannot see gets a declaration (a Window augmentation, a typed
// builder) instead.
language js

or {
  `$value as never`,
  `$value as unknown as $type`
} as $escape where { register_diagnostic(span=$escape, message="Declare the type the value has instead of casting through never or unknown.") }
